  "grafo_evidencia": {
    "nodes": [
      {
        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "1c80e5de-514f-5dec-a369-6fc1905553af",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Works: Alice or the Last Escapade, Alice's Adventures in Wonderland, Through the Looking-Glass, Jabberwocky, The Hunting of the Snark\n- People: Claude Chabrol, Lewis Carroll, Alice Carroll\n- Topics: literary nonsense, adaptation and inspiration\n\nFacts:\n- In 1977, Claude Chabrol wrote and directed the film \"Alice or the Last Escapade\" (French: \"Alice ou la dernière fugue\").\n- \"Alice or the Last Escapade\" is very loosely inspired by Lewis Carroll's \"Alice's Adventures in Wonderland\".\n- The protagonist of \"Alice or the Last Escapade\" is named Alice Carroll, combining the Alice character's name with Lewis Carroll's pseudonymous surname.\n- Lewis Carroll's best-known writings include \"Alice's Adventures in Wonderland\", its sequel \"Through the Looking-Glass\", the poem \"Jabberwocky\" contained in that sequel, and the poem \"The Hunting of the Snark\".\n- \"Alice's Adventures in Wonderland\", \"Through the Looking-Glass\", and \"The Hunting of the Snark\" are examples of literary nonsense.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "cb9b1c61-7632-5d92-8a4f-bae5c18b064a",
        "text": "Page: Alice or the Last Escapade. Sentence: Alice or the Last Escapade (French: \"Alice ou la dernière fugue\" ) is a 1977 film written and directed by Claude Chabrol.\nPage: Alice or the Last Escapade. Sentence: The film is very loosely inspired by \"Alice's Adventures in Wonderland\" by Lewis Carroll, including the protagonist's name being Alice Carroll (a combination of the Alice character and the author's pseudonymous surname).\nPage: Lewis Carroll. Sentence: His most famous writings are \"Alice's Adventures in Wonderland\", its sequel \"Through the Looking-Glass\", which includes the poem \"Jabberwocky\", and the poem \"The Hunting of the Snark\", all examples of the genre of literary nonsense.",
